		<script file="driver.lua" encryption="0"></script>
		<commands>
			<command>
				<name>SEND_KEY</name>
				<description>Send a raw Samsung key code to the TV (e.g. KEY_HOME, KEY_HDMI1)</description>
				<params>
					<param>
						<name>KeyCode</name>
						<type>STRING</type>
					</param>
				</params>
			</command>
			<command>
				<name>LAUNCH_APP</name>
				<description>Launch a TV app by name (Netflix, YouTube, Prime Video, Disney+, Apple TV, Spotify, DAZN, RaiPlay, Paramount+)</description>
				<params>
					<param>
						<name>AppName</name>
						<type>STRING</type>
					</param>
				</params>
			</command>
		</commands>
		<documentation file="www/documentation.rtf">SAMSUNG TV (WebSocket) - Unofficial Control4 driver for Samsung Tizen Smart TVs.
SETUP: 1) set IP Address; 2) set Pairing to "Pair with TV" and accept the popup on the TV; 3) bind the MiniApp drivers to the MiniApp slots for the Watch experience.
Full guide (IT/EN): www/documentation.rtf and https://github.com/DidyMond/Control4-Samsung-TV-WebSocket</documentation>
		<identify_text>Unofficial Samsung Tizen driver (WebSocket). Pair from the Pairing property.</identify_text>
